  "id": "The_Beginning_of_the_End_of_Social_Engineering_txt_31",
  "content": "Critics will rightly point out that attackers will simply use AI to attack AI. They probably will. But, again, history suggests that scale matters. When antivirus systems became ubiquitous, they did not eliminate malicious code. They changed the environment in which attackers operated. Millions of defensive systems continuously monitored, detected, shared signatures, and updated protections. The result was not perfect security but a dramatic increase in the cost and complexity of successful attacks.",
